## Android Auto

Android Auto binds `BibleAlarmMediaLibraryService`. Browse data comes from Fluxor
through `Media3LibraryCatalog` and `AndroidAutoScheduleHelper`. The library
callback allows the browse root only for a car host package. Any connected
controller can send playback commands. The browse service is what keeps the app
listed when playback is stopped. Default-schedule metadata is published only
when nothing is playing and `CarConnectionHelper.IsCarConnected()` is true.

**Why no CarAppService:** Google Play does not allow an app to declare both
`android.media.browse.MediaBrowserService` and `androidx.car.app.CarAppService`
at the same time. Media apps declare the browse action on the library service.

